  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: Number of gram equivalents of \\(\\mathrm{HCl}\\)\n\\(=\\frac{100 \\times 0.1}{1000}=0.01\\)\nNumber of gram equivalents of metal carbonate required for neutralisation must also be 0.01 . Thus, mass of 1 gram eqivalent of carbonate salt \\(\\frac{2}{0.01}=200 \\mathrm{~g}\\)\n\\(\\therefore\\) Equivalent mass of carbonate salt \\(=200\\)",
    "image": null
